course: dictionary
lesson: 7859
title: Raid: a sudden attack or a grab
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A raid is a sudden attack or a surprise visit. Read the words around it to find the clues. «Army ants raid in a moving carpet of hundreds of thousands» tells you the ants move fast, in huge numbers, and without warning, so raid must mean a sudden attack.
explain: Raid can also be a verb, a word for an action. «Matabele ants of Africa raid termites» means the ants attack the termites. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «Matabele ants of Africa attack termites» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: In everyday talk, raid can sound friendly. «Stop raiding the biscuit tin!» does not mean an attack. It means taking a lot of biscuits quickly. The words around the word show you which meaning fits, so always read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Context also shows how serious a raid is. «Police raid the house at dawn» tells you the police arrived early in the morning to search it. «Viking raiders» tells you the Vikings were people who made sudden attacks from the sea.
fact: A raid is a sudden attack on a place, or a surprise visit by police to search it.
fact: As a verb, «raid» means to attack a place, or to take a lot from something quickly.
fact: «Vikings» were Norse people from Denmark, Norway and Sweden, and viking really meant going on a sea raid.
fact: «Raid the fridge» is informal and means to take a lot of food from it.
fact: In online games, a raid is when many players team up to beat a big enemy.
exercise: «Army ants raid in a moving carpet of hundreds of thousands.» What does raid mean here? | Sleeping quietly in a nest | A slow walk to the park | *A sudden attack | Painting a bright pattern
exercise: Ella says, «I'm going to raid the fridge after school.» What does she mean? | *She will take a lot of food from it | She will paint the fridge blue | She will break the fridge with a hammer | She will sleep beside the fridge
exercise: Which meaning of raid fits «a bank raid»? | A quiet walk to the bank | A visit to count the money with the manager | A party held in the bank | *A sudden break-in by robbers to steal
test: What does police raid mean in «Police raid the house at dawn»? | *Police make a surprise visit to search it | Police go to sleep in it | Police paint the house | Police sell the house
test: Your mum says, «Stop raiding the biscuit tin!» What does raiding mean? | Hiding it under the bed | Cleaning it carefully | *Taking a lot from it quickly | Painting it blue
exam: What is a raider, from «Viking raiders» in the history lesson? | A teacher of history | A fisher who sells fish at market | *A person who makes sudden attacks on places | A farmer who grows barley
